{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["The reason for <b>And Abram fell on his face</b> is to focus his mind for prophecy. And when the prophecy concerning the commandment of circumcision was completed for him, Abraham arose and stood, and the divine speech came to him a second time from heaven, and He said to him, \"As for Sarai your wife,\" etc., and he again fell on his face to focus his mind, and he prayed on behalf of Ishmael, in the manner of \"And they fell on their faces and said, O El, Elohim of the spirits,\" etc. (Numbers 16:22), and likewise, \"and I shall consume them in a moment, and they fell on their faces\" (ibid. 17:10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:09.847071156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}